{"success": true, "path": "build_system_notes.txt", "content": "build_system_notes.txt (partial draft)

Notes on migrating our build from Maven to Gradle. Converted the POM, switched to the built-in test task, and pinned a guava/gson version conflict. Build times improved: clean builds roughly halved, and incremental builds are much faster now. The remote build cache helped a lot with rebuilds across the team.

We run CI on cloud machines. The provider sends us some sustainability reports each quarter, and there has been general discussion at the org level about making our builds greener. It would be interesting someday to quantify how much energy our CI fleet uses in the cloud, but we haven't tracked those numbers yet. I remember reading that data centers in general use a lot of electricity for cooling, but I don't have figures for our provider. Maybe once the migration is fully rolled out we can ask the platform team for energy dashboards and right-size the agent instances.", "provenance": "insufficient_source", "event_id": "E1"}

